      "text": "Day 19 - Redux: \ni learnt react-redux and redux-toolkit:\nfirst i installed on my project redux using command\nnpm i @redux.js/toolkit react-redux\nredux is a state management liberary to manage state. \nFirst I created store.jsx for store all reducer inside store.\nthen i creaed countSlice.jsx for reducers/action of countslice\nslice is a action. for creating countSlice i need createSlice\nmethod so i create const countSlice = createSlice({});\ninside createSlice one object and inside object first name, \ninitialState, and reducers/action. inside reducers take a\nobject and inside object we can give operations like couter\nopeartion increment, decrement. every operation give a\ncallback inside callback two argument state, action. state is\ninitial value and action take user given value from ui. \nafter all operation we need to export slice actions and slice.\nfor actions we use countSlice.actions and for slice we default\nexport using countSlice.reducer. Then on store we register\nour slice inside reducer object using key. like count:\ncountReducer. \nthis is couterSlice.jsx code:\nimport { createSlice } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\n\nconst countSlice = createSlice({\n    name: 'count', \n    initialState: {\n        count: 0,\n    },\n    reducers: {\n        increment: (state, action) => {\n            state.count++;\n            console.log(action)\n        },\n        decrement: (state) => {\n            state.count--;\n        }\n    }\n})\nconsole.log(countSlice);\n  \nexport const {increment, decrement} = countSlice.actions;\nexport default countSlice.reducer\n\non creatation of store and slice @reduxjs/toolkit import\nstatement work, and at the time of delivery mean providing\nredux on our project we use react-redux. now we provide\nstore on our app.jsx for that.\nI used <provider store={store}><app/><provider/>  inside\nprovider store i pass as a props. \n\nthis is store.jsx code:\nimport { configureStore } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\nimport counterReducer from '../features/CountSlice'\nimport cartReducer from '../features/cartItemSlice'\n\nexport const store = configureStore({\n    reducer: {\n        count: counterReducer,\n        cart: cartReducer,\n    }\n})\n\n\nin redux two thing useDispatch() hook for action call, and\nuseSelector() hook for get state data from redux. \non app.jsx i created twon button one for increment and 2nd\nfor decrement, and on button add onclick event listener\nthen give a callback function and and called increment\nfunction inside dispatch(increment()) and same for decrement\nbutton dispatch(decrement()). and using useSelector() \nconst {count} = useSelector((store) => store.count) \nuseSelector() alse need a callback inside store as a argunt \nstore.count give count state value. and i show count in \nh1 tag like <h1> {count} <h1/> and when i clicked on increment\nthen coutn value show 0 to 1 same when click on decrement\nbutton it's show 1 to 0. \n\nthis is app.jsx code:\nimport React from \"react\";\nimport { useDispatch, useSelector } from \"react-redux\";\nimport { store } from \"./apps/Store\";\nimport { decrement, increment } from \"./features/CountSlice\";\nimport About from \"./pages/About\";\n\nconst App = () => {\n  const dispatch = useDispatch();\n  let { count } = useSelector((store) => store.count);\n  console.log(\"hello\");\n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4  flex flex-col justify-center items-\ncenter gap-5 text-2xl h-screen bg-black text-white\">\n      Redux Toolkit:\n      <h1>Count: {count}</h1>\n      <div className=\"flex gap-5\">\n        <button\n          className=\"bg-red-500 rounded-xl px-2 py-1\"\n          onClick={() => dispatch(increment(\"argument\"))}\n        >\n          Increment\n        </button>\n        <button\n          className=\"bg-red-500 rounded-xl px-2 py-1\"\n          onClick={() => dispatch(decrement())}\n        >\n          Decrement\n        </button>\n      </div>\n      <About />\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default App;\n\n\nalso i created cartItemSlice.jsx for cart item:\nimport { createSlice } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\n\nconst cartSlice = createSlice({\n    name: \"cart\", \n    initialState: {\n        cartItems: null\n    },\n    reducers: {\n        addCart: (state, action) => {\n            state.cartItems = action.payload;\n        },\n        removeCart: () => {}\n    }\n})\n\nexport const {addCart, removeCart} = cartSlice.actions;\nexport default cartSlice.reducer;\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Day 19 - Redux: \ni learnt react-redux and redux-toolkit:\nfirst i installed on my project redux using command\nnpm i @redux.js/toolkit react-redux\nredux is a state management liberary to manage state. \nFirst I created store.jsx for store all reducer inside store.\nthen i creaed countSlice.jsx for reducers/action of countslice \nslice is a action. for creating countSlice i need createSlice method so i create const countSlice = createSlice({});\ninside createSlice one object and inside object first name, \ninitialState, and reducers/action. inside reducers take a object and inside object we can give operations like couter\nopeartion increment, decrement. every operation give a callback inside callback two argument state, action. state is\ninitial value and action take user given value from ui. \nafter all operation we need to export slice actions and slice.\nfor actions we use countSlice.actions and for slice we default\nexport using countSlice.reducer. Then on store we register our slice inside reducer object using key. like count: countReducer. \nthis is couterSlice.jsx code:\nimport { createSlice } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\n\nconst countSlice = createSlice({\n    name: 'count', \n    initialState: {\n        count: 0,\n    },\n    reducers: {\n        increment: (state, action) => {\n            state.count++;\n            console.log(action)\n        },\n        decrement: (state) => {\n            state.count--;\n        }\n    }\n})\nconsole.log(countSlice);\n  \nexport const {increment, decrement} = countSlice.actions;\nexport default countSlice.reducer\n\non creatation of store and slice @reduxjs/toolkit import statement work, and at the time of delivery mean providing redux on our project we use react-redux. now we provide store on our app.jsx for that.\nI used <provider store={store}><app/><provider/>  inside\nprovider store i pass as a props. \n\nthis is store.jsx code:\nimport { configureStore } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\nimport counterReducer from '../features/CountSlice'\nimport cartReducer from '../features/cartItemSlice'\n\nexport const store = configureStore({\n    reducer: {\n        count: counterReducer,\n        cart: cartReducer,\n    }\n})\n\n\nin redux two thing useDispatch() hook for action call, and useSelector() hook for get state data from redux. \non app.jsx i created twon button one for increment and 2nd\nfor decrement, and on button add onclick event listener\nthen give a callback function and and called increment function inside dispatch(increment()) and same for decrement\nbutton dispatch(decrement()). and using useSelector() \nconst {count} = useSelector((store) => store.count) \nuseSelector() alse need a callback inside store as a argunt \nstore.count give count state value. and i show count in \nh1 tag like <h1> {count} <h1/> and when i clicked on increment\nthen coutn value show 0 to 1 same when click on decrement\nbutton it's show 1 to 0. \n\nthis is app.jsx code:\nimport React from \"react\";\nimport { useDispatch, useSelector } from \"react-redux\";\nimport { store } from \"./apps/Store\";\nimport { decrement, increment } from \"./features/CountSlice\";\nimport About from \"./pages/About\";\n\nconst App = () => {\n  const dispatch = useDispatch();\n  let { count } = useSelector((store) => store.count);\n  console.log(\"hello\");\n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4  flex flex-col justify-center items-center gap-5 text-2xl h-screen bg-black text-white\">\n      Redux Toolkit:\n      <h1>Count: {count}</h1>\n      <div className=\"flex gap-5\">\n        <button\n          className=\"bg-red-500 rounded-xl px-2 py-1\"\n          onClick={() => dispatch(increment(\"argument\"))}\n        >\n          Increment\n        </button>\n        <button\n          className=\"bg-red-500 rounded-xl px-2 py-1\"\n          onClick={() => dispatch(decrement())}\n        >\n          Decrement\n        </button>\n      </div>\n      <About />\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default App;\n\n\nalso i created cartItemSlice.jsx for cart item:\nimport { createSlice } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\n\nconst cartSlice = createSlice({\n    name: \"cart\", \n    initialState: {\n        cartItems: null\n    },\n    reducers: {\n        addCart: (state, action) => {\n            state.cartItems = action.payload;\n        },\n        removeCart: () => {}\n    }\n})\n\nexport const {addCart, removeCart} = cartSlice.actions;\nexport default cartSlice.reducer;\n\n\n\n\n",
